<title>FRANCE: Pernod Ricard sales rise.</title>
<headline>Pernod Ricard sales rise.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Twelve months to Dec 31, 1996.</p>
<p>(All figures in millions of French francs)</p>
<p>    Turnover					16,818    up   5.5 pct</p>
<p>NOTE - Groupe Pernod Ricard said in a statement that stripping out structural changes and exchange rate fluctuations, sales rose by 5.2 percent. Turnover growth was helped by a 7.4 percent rise in sales of wines and spirits outside France. In France, sales were up 4.8 percent. It said sales benefited from favourable currency developments. The results, it said, underlined the growing internationalisation of its operations with 62.3 percent of sales derived from abroad, compared with 61.2 percent in 1995.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
